>  <SOURCE_REFERENCES>
["https://doi.org/10.1002/wcms.1606","https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.8b01176","https://doi.org/10.1021/ic3007525","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/csd_smiles.csv","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/tmqmg_smiles.csv","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQM/tree/ece824419c9006fe66436daf233822b75533b82f/tmQM","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQMg/tree/e1dc9887b8f20a217a1db6ca972d726bcbaab45b","https://www.crystallography.net/cod/4329639.cif"]

>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. The terminal oxo is O²⁻, Isopropoxide carries −1. Assign the conjugated nitrogen ligand a charge of −2 for the supplied H23 composition. The carbonyl, phenoxide and carbanion give one delocalized limiting form. V(V) balances the total charge. Localized 6 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

>  <UPSTREAM_COMPARISON>
Equivalent

